    "**Answer to task A1:** The decay rate \\(k\\) controls how quickly the tracer concentration decreases, with a larger \\(k\\) causing faster decay and a smaller \\(k\\) causing slower decay.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer to task A2:** The numerical curve first visibly disagreed with the exact solution at \\(dt = 2.0\\) days.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer to task A3:** The largest time step that still gives a non-negative curve is \\(dt = 1.0\\).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer to task A4:** When \\(k\\,dt>1\\), the update rule \\(C_{\\text{new}}=C_{\\text{old}}(1-k\\,dt)\\) multiplies the old concentration by a negative value. This means the numerical method removes more tracer than is present during one step, causing the concentration to overshoot below zero.\n",
